# Data access

Reads and writes of `decks` and `cards` stay on the server and go through
helper functions in `src/db/queries/`. A page, layout, Server Action, Route
Handler, or Client Component never imports `db`, never imports `decks` or
`cards` to build a query, and never calls `select`, `insert`, `update`, or
`delete`. A Client Component never calls `fetch` for app data.
[src/index.ts](mdc:src/index.ts) is the seed script only; it is the one place
a write may run outside a Server Action, and it may keep its own Drizzle
client.

Ownership still comes from `auth()` as described in
[.cursor/rules/clerk.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/clerk.mdc). The caller passes that
`userId` into the helper. Zod checks the shape of input. It does not decide
who owns a row. Inside a helper, build the query as described in
[.cursor/rules/drizzle.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/drizzle.mdc).

## Queries

Put one module per table in `src/db/queries/`: `decks.ts` and `cards.ts`.
Each helper imports `db` from [src/db/index.ts](mdc:src/db/index.ts) and the
table from [src/db/schema.ts](mdc:src/db/schema.ts). A helper takes plain
arguments (`userId`, ids, and column values) and returns rows. It does not
call `auth()`, read `FormData`, or validate with Zod.

Every helper that reads or writes `decks` includes `eq(decks.userId, userId)`.
Every helper that reads or writes `cards` checks that the parent deck matches
both the deck id and `eq(decks.userId, userId)`. If that check matches
nothing, return no row. Do not query by id alone.

```ts
import { desc, eq } from "drizzle-orm"
import { db } from "@/src/db"
import { decks } from "@/src/db/schema"

export async function getDecksByUserId(userId: string) {
  return db
    .select()
    .from(decks)
    .where(eq(decks.userId, userId))
    .orderBy(desc(decks.updatedAt))
}

export async function insertDeck(values: {
  userId: string
  name: string
  description: string | null
}) {
  return db.insert(decks).values(values).returning()
}
```

## Reads

Load `decks` and `cards` by calling those helpers from Server Components
(pages, layouts, or async server-only helpers they call). Pass the result
into Client Components as props. Do not load this data from a Client
Component, a Route Handler, or a Server Action whose only job is to return
rows.

## Writes

Every `insert`, `update`, and `delete` of `decks` or `cards` is a helper in
`src/db/queries/`, called from a Server Action. Put `'use server'` at the top
of the action file. Do not mutate those tables from a Route Handler, a Server
Component render, or client code.

## Validation

Validate with Zod from the `zod` package. Do not hand-check fields with
`if` statements, and do not trust values because TypeScript already describes
them.

Every value passed into a Server Action has a TypeScript type derived from its
Zod schema. The action parameter is that type. It is never `FormData`, and the
action does not read fields with `formData.get`. A Client Component builds a
plain object and passes that object.

Parse the argument with `safeParse` before any write. Use `parsed.data` when
calling the query helper. When parsing fails, return the validation error and
do not write.

```ts
'use server'

import { z } from 'zod'
import { insertDeck } from '@/src/db/queries/decks'

const createDeckSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().trim().min(1),
  description: z.string().trim().optional(),
})

type CreateDeckInput = z.infer<typeof createDeckSchema>

export async function createDeck(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  const parsed = createDeckSchema.safeParse(input)
  if (!parsed.success) {
    return { error: parsed.error.flatten() }
  }

  const { name, description } = parsed.data
  // userId comes from auth(); then call insertDeck({ userId, name, description })
}
```
